%U A399164 603477474099,2572004475857,10961812673645,46718945561710,199114867164801,848622113563901
%N A399164 Number of fixed point free involutions in S_{2n} (or perfect matchings on [2n]) which avoid the patterns {123, 132, 321}.
%C A399164 a(n) is the number of perfect matchings on [2n] that simultaneously avoid the patterns 123, 132, and 321, where pattern avoidance for matchings is in the sense of Bloom and Elizalde.
%C A399164 The term a(0)=1 corresponds to the empty matching.
%H A399164 Sucharita Biswas, Umesh Shankar and Sivaramakrishnan Sivasubramanian, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.08562">Matchings and shape-Wilf-Equivalence of sets of patterns of length three I: Triples</a>, arXiv:2609.08562 [math.CO], 2026. See Theorem 24.
%F A399164 G.f.: (1 - 3*x - 3*x^2 + 2*x^3)/(1 - 4*x - 2*x^2 + 4*x^3 - x^4).
%F A399164 a(0)=1, a(1)=1, a(2)=3, a(3)=12, and for n >= 4, a(n) = 4*a(n-1) + 2*a(n-2) - 4*a(n-3) + a(n-4).
%F A399164 The characteristic polynomial of the recurrence is x^4 - 4*x^3 - 2*x^2 + 4*x - 1.
%Y A399164 Cf. A399989 (avoiding the patterns 132, 312, and 321).
%K A399164 nonn,easy,new
%O A399164 0,3
